    "q-161200": {
      "dom_id": "step-q161200",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F$ and the surface $S$ with unit normal vector $n,$ where\n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=⟨xy,\\,yz,\\,xz⟩\\,,\\,n(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,2⟩\\,.\n$$\n\nIf the flux of $F$ across $S$ with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}{∬}_{S}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}S,\n$$\n\nwhat is the missing expression?",
      "worked_solution": "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nCalculating the dot product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨xy,\\,yz,\\,xz⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨xy,\\,yz,\\,xz⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}(xy-yz+2xz) \\\\  & =\\frac{xy-yz+2xz}{\\sqrt{6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\frac{xy-yz+2xz}{\\sqrt{6}}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}{∬}_{S}xy-yz+2xz\\,\\text{d}S.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
