    "q-162158": {
      "dom_id": "step-q162158",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=⟨z+5,\\,x-2y,\\,3x-2y⟩$ and a finite region $S$ of the plane $z=x+2y+1$ such that $\\text{Area}(S)=\\sqrt{2}.$ Calculate the flux of $F$ through $S$ with respect to the *downward*-pointing unit normal vector $n.$",
      "worked_solution": "If $S$ is an oriented surface with unit normal vector $n,$ and $F$ is continuous vector field, then the flux of $F$ across $S$ measured with respect to $n$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nNotice that our surface $z=x+2y+1$ can be written using the dot product as \n\n$$\n⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩\\cdot {{⟨-1,\\,-2,\\,1⟩}_{⏟}}_{\\overset{~}{n}}=1,\\,\\text{or}\\,⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩\\cdot {{⟨1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩}_{⏟}}_{-\\overset{~}{n}}=-1.\n$$\n\nSince we require a downward-pointing normal vector to our surface $S,$ we must select one where the $z$-component is negative. This gives us the normal vector\n\n$$\n\\overset{~}{n}=⟨1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩.\n$$\n\nNormalizing this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =\\frac{\\overset{~}{n}}{‖\\overset{~}{n}‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{⟨1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $z=x+2y+1$ on $S,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F\\cdot n & =⟨z+5,\\,x-2y,\\,3x-2y⟩\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨x+2y+6,\\,x-2y,\\,3x-2y⟩\\cdot ⟨1,\\,2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}((x+2y+6)+2(x-2y)-(3x-2y)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}(x+2y+6+2x-4y-3x+2y) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the flux of $F$ across $S$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{S}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{S}\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}{∬}_{S}\\,\\text{d}S \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\text{Area}(S) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
